    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by the dual-threat upside of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.41). Both players benefit from facing pitchers with favorable xERAs\u2014Burrows (4.71) and Pfaadt (4.59)\u2014but it is their stolen base potential against pitchers with slow deliveries that elevates them to the top of our daily projections. **Jackson Merrill** is a particularly strong play; he maximizes his 86% SB success rate against Pfaadt, and the favorable platoon dynamic provides the volume necessary to chase category production in this 5x5 format. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** sees a massive 17% boost from the opposing SP skill, making him our primary engine for the afternoon.\n\nWhile **Kyle Tucker** (67.05) remains a cornerstone, the real value of the lineup lies in the middle-order efficiency provided by **Andy Pages** (62.29) and **Curtis Mead** (62.15). Both capitalize on positive platoon splits against Freeland and Burrows respectively. The most difficult decision today involved **Drake Baldwin** (59.20); while his score sits just below the \"Strong\" threshold, his presence at the #4 spot in the order gives him enough RBI potential to justify the start despite a neutral platoon against Peralta. **Heliot Ramos** (50.83) serves as our most volatile piece; his lead-off assignment provides a vital boost, though he faces a stiff test against the elite delivery of Gausman. We are closely monitoring the status of our depth, as **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** remain sidelined, while **Gunnar Henderson** is inactive due to a scheduled team off-day. We continue to hold **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Liam Hicks**, **Denzer Guzman**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Cole Carrigg** in reserve as we navigate this stretch of the season.",
